            <Node Bounds="235,382,58,19" Id="DGSxlqETIg6LFNCUrrzZDA">
              <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="CMiX.Engine.BindChannel" LastDependency="CMiX_ENGINE.Definitions.vl">
                <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
                <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="Keyspace" />
              </p:NodeReference>
              <Pin Id="OO40ttQ9qgpLGXBZxgXoJZ" Name="Node Context" Kind="InputPin" IsHidden="true" />
              <Pin Id="MfdT7HvEorMLBIVhTpVP4y" Name="Input" Kind="InputPin" />
              <Pin Id="Dk7P9c5uAYVM9Gk7tPnDPe" Name="Output" Kind="OutputPin" />
              <Pin Id="CorIuJr90upPD8qdO2HZXr" Name="Prefix" Kind="InputPin" />
            </Node>
            <ControlPoint Id="MnoYUCc2qgSMRPPqtJrAgb" Bounds="290,371" />
            <Pad Id="CixYzvXEx7MO9giCXZg6OY" Comment="Latency" Bounds="137,500,35,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
            <Pad Id="Hb8sXU9RQfALNBnHl1JBqx" Bounds="467,529,584,286" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="gregsn's explanation:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Pub-Sub-based value-binding for public channels which refines the way how received values on the client get sampled. For this a couple of values get queued together with time-stamps. This allows to sample values from the past instead of always showing the latest value.&#xD;&#xA;It's like a very small timeline allowing you to sample for t = currentTime - 0.05s for example.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The final tweak that makes this robust is to reason about frame times.&#xD;&#xA;PTP and frame sync lead to a situation where all machines have frame times ft = n / 60 + C, where C is a random offset which is vvvery similar for all machines due to PTP and frame sync.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Sampling that timeline now needs to be done in a way that tiny variations in C don't lead to selecting a different value.&#xD;&#xA;So we need to get the nearest for t - x frames. Nearest is a tad older or a tad newer, but closest to the desired sampling time.">
              <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
                <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
              </p:TypeAnnotation>
              <p:ValueBoxSettings>
                <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
                <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
              </p:ValueBoxSettings>
            </Pad>
          </Canvas>
